.IX Title "Lucy::Analysis::Token 3pm"
.TH Lucy::Analysis::Token 3pm 2026-09-16 "perl v5.40.1" "User Contributed Perl Documentation"
.\" For nroff, turn off justification.  Always turn off hyphenation; it makes
.\" way too many mistakes in technical documents.
.if n .ad l
.nh
.SH NAME
Lucy::Analysis::Token \- Unit of text.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IX Header "SYNOPSIS"
.Vb 5
\&        my $token = Lucy::Analysis::Token\->new(
\&            text         => \*(Aqblind\*(Aq,
\&            start_offset => 8,
\&            end_offset   => 13,
\&        );
\&
\&        $token\->set_text(\*(Aqmice\*(Aq);
.Ve
.SH DESCRIPTION
.IX Header "DESCRIPTION"
Token is the fundamental unit used by Lucy’s Analyzer subclasses.
Each Token has 5 attributes: \f(CW\*(C`text\*(C'\fR, \f(CW\*(C`start_offset\*(C'\fR,
\&\f(CW\*(C`end_offset\*(C'\fR, \f(CW\*(C`boost\*(C'\fR, and \f(CW\*(C`pos_inc\*(C'\fR.
.PP
The \f(CW\*(C`text\*(C'\fR attribute is a Unicode string encoded as UTF\-8.
.PP
\&\f(CW\*(C`start_offset\*(C'\fR is the start point of the token text, measured in
Unicode code points from the top of the stored field;
\&\f(CW\*(C`end_offset\*(C'\fR delimits the corresponding closing boundary.
\&\f(CW\*(C`start_offset\*(C'\fR and \f(CW\*(C`end_offset\*(C'\fR locate the Token
within a larger context, even if the Token’s text attribute gets modified
– by stemming, for instance.  The Token for “beating” in the text “beating
a dead horse” begins life with a start_offset of 0 and an end_offset of 7;
after stemming, the text is “beat”, but the start_offset is still 0 and the
end_offset is still 7.  This allows “beating” to be highlighted correctly
after a search matches “beat”.
.PP
\&\f(CW\*(C`boost\*(C'\fR is a per-token weight.  Use this when you want to assign
more or less importance to a particular token, as you might for emboldened
text within an HTML document, for example.  (Note: The field this token
belongs to must be spec’d to use a posting of type RichPosting.)
.PP
\&\f(CW\*(C`pos_inc\*(C'\fR is the POSition INCrement, measured in Tokens.  This
attribute, which defaults to 1, is a an advanced tool for manipulating
phrase matching.  Ordinarily, Tokens are assigned consecutive position
numbers: 0, 1, and 2 for \f(CW"three blind mice"\fR.  However, if you
set the position increment for “blind” to, say, 1000, then the three tokens
will end up assigned to positions 0, 1, and 1001 – and will no longer
produce a phrase match for the query \f(CW"three blind mice"\fR.
.SH CONSTRUCTORS
.IX Header "CONSTRUCTORS"
.SS new
.IX Subsection "new"
.Vb 7
\&    my $token = Lucy::Analysis::Token\->new(
\&        text         => $text,          # required
\&        start_offset => $start_offset,  # required
\&        end_offset   => $end_offset,    # required
\&        boost        => 1.0,            # optional
\&        pos_inc      => 1,              # optional
\&    );
.Ve
.IP \(bu 4
\&\fBtext\fR \- A string.
.IP \(bu 4
\&\fBstart_offset\fR \- Start offset into the original document in Unicode
code points.
.IP \(bu 4
\&\fBstart_offset\fR \- End offset into the original document in Unicode
code points.
.IP \(bu 4
\&\fBboost\fR \- Per-token weight.
.IP \(bu 4
\&\fBpos_inc\fR \- Position increment for phrase matching.
.SH METHODS
.IX Header "METHODS"
.SS get_text
.IX Subsection "get_text"
.Vb 1
\&    my $text = $token\->get_text;
.Ve
.PP
Get the token's text.
.SS set_text
.IX Subsection "set_text"
.Vb 1
\&    $token\->set_text($text);
.Ve
.PP
Set the token's text.
.SS get_start_offset
.IX Subsection "get_start_offset"
.Vb 1
\&    my $int = $token\->get_start_offset();
.Ve
.SS get_end_offset
.IX Subsection "get_end_offset"
.Vb 1
\&    my $int = $token\->get_end_offset();
.Ve
.SS get_boost
.IX Subsection "get_boost"
.Vb 1
\&    my $float = $token\->get_boost();
.Ve
.SS get_pos_inc
.IX Subsection "get_pos_inc"
.Vb 1
\&    my $int = $token\->get_pos_inc();
.Ve
.SS get_len
.IX Subsection "get_len"
.Vb 1
\&    my $int = $token\->get_len();
.Ve
.SH INHERITANCE
.IX Header "INHERITANCE"
Lucy::Analysis::Token isa Clownfish::Obj.
